+## Turn usage — issue #93
+
+The hook retains a single optional usage argument, now a turn total. A per-round breakdown is rejected for this change because billing and budgeting need a total and no consumer requirement justifies a wider public surface. The public hook signature must name the argument `totalUsage` so its scope is visible without reading the orchestrator. This behaviour change requires a MINOR version bump and a changelog entry explaining that existing consumers record larger counts for tool-heavy turns.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the sum of input, output and total tokens from every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final answer; totals are isolated per turn and a no-tool turn retains its original usage ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call across two tool rounds once per turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L63)).
+- Missing usage in any round is ignored while all reported rounds are summed; if no round reports usage the hook receives `undefined`, while explicitly reported zero counts remain zero ([validated by: sums reported rounds despite missing usage and leaves wholly unreported turns undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L77)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The following error-handling property remains outside issue #93.
 
-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error`, so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
